+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "maxTurns: 5,",
+  "cause": "The customer-facing `triage` agent, which runs every support chat turn, was defined without a `store`, so its conversation was never persisted as a server snapshot and could not be resumed by session id.",
+  "evidence": "Before the fix, `triage.loadChat({ sessionId })` threw \"FAILED_PRECONDITION: getSnapshotData requires a persistent store. Provide a 'store' when defining 'triage'.\"; `refundAgent`, which has `store`, did not throw that error. After adding `store,` to `triage` (same `FileSessionStore` as `refundAgent`), `tsc --noEmit` passes, and a scratch two-turn run (\"My order is A-1001.\" then `triage.loadChat({ sessionId })` with \"What is its status?\") answered with A-1001's status, ETA and tracking code on turn two."
+}
